{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":100040,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2023-06-09T14:43:39.109Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eDraft PEP: \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0715/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 715 – Disabling bdist_egg distribution uploads on PyPI | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOther context:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrevious deprecations of underused filetypes and suffixes: \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0527/\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 527 – Removing Un(der)used file types/extensions on PyPI | peps.python.org\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrevious DPO thread on deprecating \u003ccode\u003e.egg\u003c/code\u003e uploads: \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/should-pypi-deprecate-egg-uploads/13364\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eShould PyPI deprecate .egg uploads?\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWarehouse (PyPI) tracking issue for deprecating \u003ccode\u003e.egg\u003c/code\u003e uploads: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/pypi/warehouse/issues/10653\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDeprecate .egg uploads · Issue #10653 · pypi/warehouse · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo summarize the rationale and motivation:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEgg distributions make up a tiny fraction of the overall number of distributions uploaded to PyPI (under 0.2%), and have been deprecated by other components of the packaging ecosystem (\u003ccode\u003epip\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003esetuptools\u003c/code\u003e, etc.) for years;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEgg distributions are effectively a non-standard legacy alternative to the other built distribution format that PyPI supports (wheels), meaning that its continued presence represents a source of potential user confusion about which format is better defined and encouraged by the broader ecosystem.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo summarize the proposed changes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI propose that we consider \u003ccode\u003ebdist_egg\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e.egg\u003c/code\u003e deprecated on PyPI and enable a 1-month deprecation period, similar to what was done with PEP 527;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAfter the deprecation period, PyPI should cease to accept uploads of egg distributions;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExisting distributions \u003cstrong\u003eare not\u003c/strong\u003e affected, meaning that PyPI will continue to serve any egg distributions uploaded before and during the deprecation period.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe PEP also enumerates some methods for communicating this change, including emailing every maintainer of every project that has uploaded an egg distribution since January 1 2023, emailing every maintainer whose project uploads an egg during the deprecation period, and posting a notice to the PyPI blog.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-06-09T14:43:39.109Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":201,"reads":113,"readers_count":112,"score":1207.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":27610,"topic_slug":"pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0715/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 715 – Disabling bdist_egg distribution uploads on PyPI | peps.python.org","clicks":30},{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0527/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 527 – Removing Un(der)used file types/extensions on PyPI | peps.python.org","clicks":4},{"url":"https://github.com/pypi/warehouse/issues/10653","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Deprecate .egg uploads · Issue #10653 · pypi/warehouse · GitHub","clicks":2},{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/should-pypi-deprecate-egg-uploads/13364","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Should PyPI deprecate .egg uploads?","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":10}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi/27610/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":10}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":10,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":100045,"name":"Paul Moore","username":"pf_moore","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/{size}/35_2.png","created_at":"2023-06-09T15:20:22.652Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eLooking at the files currently on PyPI, I see the following extensions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003e{'.bz2', '.tgz', '.exe', '.tar.gz', '.msi', '.egg', '.rpm', '.ZIP', '.deb', '.whl', '.dmg', '.zip'}\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOf these, I believe the only ones that will still be accepted after PEP 715 is implemented would be \u003ccode\u003e.tar.gz\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e.zip\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e.whl\u003c/code\u003e (the uppercase \u003ccode\u003e.ZIP\u003c/code\u003e is a single file \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/project/notebook/4.0.5/#files\"\u003efrom 2015\u003c/a\u003e, presumably incorrectly named). Is that correct? And would it be worth documenting that explicitly somewhere?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-06-09T15:20:22.652Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":29,"reads":107,"readers_count":106,"score":161.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":27610,"topic_slug":"pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi","display_username":"Paul Moore","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://pypi.org/project/notebook/4.0.5/#files","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"notebook · PyPI","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":"CPython core developer","title_is_group":true,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":35,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi/27610/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":100047,"name":"William Woodruff","username":"woodruffw","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/woodruffw/{size}/37228_2.png","created_at":"2023-06-09T15:24:37.219Z","cooked":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI believe the only ones that will still be accepted after PEP 715 is implemented would be \u003ccode\u003e.tar.gz\u003c/code\u003e , \u003ccode\u003e.zip\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e.whl\u003c/code\u003e (the uppercase \u003ccode\u003e.ZIP\u003c/code\u003e is a single file \u003ca href=\"https://pypi.org/project/notebook/4.0.5/#files\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003efrom 2015\u003c/a\u003e, presumably incorrectly named). Is that correct?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s my understanding as well!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can make that explicit in this PEP, if you think that makes sense – PEP 527 does something similar with the filetypes/extensions that it deprecated.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeyond that, maybe it makes sense to update the PyPUG documentation around support? The current section on uploading to PyPI is somewhat sparse (and doesn’t mention which filetypes are supported at all): \u003ca href=\"https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/distributing-packages-using-setuptools/#uploading-your-project-to-pypi\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePackaging and distributing projects - Python Packaging User Guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-06-09T15:24:37.219Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":105,"readers_count":104,"score":41.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":27610,"topic_slug":"pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi","display_username":"William Woodruff","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/distributing-packages-using-setuptools/#uploading-your-project-to-pypi","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Packaging and distributing projects — Python Packaging User Guide","clicks":2},{"url":"https://pypi.org/project/notebook/4.0.5/#files","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"notebook · PyPI","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":35,"username":"pf_moore","name":"Paul Moore","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pf_moore/{size}/35_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":994,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi/27610/3","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":100317,"name":"Donald Stufft","username":"dstufft","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/dstufft/{size}/23_2.png","created_at":"2023-06-12T02:20:33.964Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m +1 on this PEP, I think it’s long been time for PyPI to drop support for the egg format unless someone comes forward with a compelling use case to delay it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-06-12T02:20:33.964Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":89,"readers_count":88,"score":62.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":27610,"topic_slug":"pep-715-disabling-bdist-egg-distribution-uploads-on-pypi","display_username":"Donald Stufft","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"r